{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Review sentencing for serious violent, sexual and child abuse offences",
        "additional_details": "We believe public confidence in justice requires sentences that deter crime and keep the public safe. We are concerned about the use of non-custodial and suspended sentences for serious offences. We believe greater oversight of sentencing trends could help protect victims and communities from harm.",
        "background": "Commission an independent inquiry into sentencing for serious violent, sexual and child abuse offences. Review the rules to make sentences for serious violent offences imposed in youth courts eligible for the Unduly Lenient Sentence scheme.",
